# The build context is the repository root, because compose builds from there,
# and backend/Dockerfile only ever COPYs out of backend/. So this is a whitelist:
# everything is excluded, backend/ is let back in, and its build output is
# excluded again. Without it every build uploaded ~500 MB — frontend/node_modules,
# backend/build with its upstream snapshots, and the stale build/ directory of
# every module, which COPY then carried into the build stage.
*
!backend/
backend/.gradle/
backend/**/build/
